*Evidence:* SnoutCraft currently offers a 24-hour preview, unlimited
revisions and refund-before-approval; House of Whiskerton similarly
promises proof-before-printing and free likeness fixes; Noble & Wag
supports unlimited revisions after a 1=E2=80=932 day proof.
*Customer problem represented:* personalized pet art has enough likeness
risk that sellers compete by removing approval risk before production.
*Current workaround:* wait for a human proof/revision cycle.
*Roast.pet implication:* generate a near-instant card/video preview before
physical fulfilment, with one-click =E2=80=9Cface/markings wrong=E2=80=9D, =
=E2=80=9Cjoke wrong=E2=80=9D,
and =E2=80=9Crecipient detail wrong=E2=80=9D revision controls.
*Occasion:* birthdays, Christmas, general pet-parent gifts.
*Independent evidence:* strong; 3+ current sellers.
*Prototype:* A/B Etsy flow: checkout directly vs upload =E2=86=92 instant
watermarked preview =E2=86=92 approve/pay/print.
2. Multi-pet support extends well beyond two pets =E2=80=94 MEDIUM/HIGH =E2=
=80=94
BUILD/TEST

*Evidence:* Noble & Wag explicitly sells matching 2-, 3- and 4-pet
products; Pawcelain supports one to five pets and distinguishes them using
coat colour, ear shape and facial markings. This independently strengthens
the earlier two-pet signal.
*Wanted/problem:* households frequently need a gift representing the whole
pet group rather than selecting one animal.
*Current workaround:* buy a dedicated multi-pet SKU or commission.
*Roast.pet implication:* do not architect identity/composition around a
permanent 1=E2=80=932 pet ceiling. V1 can price 1 pet / 2 pets / =E2=80=9Cw=
hole gang=E2=80=9D while
the scene system supports more.
*Occasion:* family birthdays, Christmas, multi-pet households.
*Prototype:* Etsy listing variant: =E2=80=9CYour Dogs Roast Dad =E2=80=94 1=
, 2 or Whole
Gang=E2=80=9D. Measure pet-count selection and upload completion.
3. Same-day digital rescue is an explicit product job =E2=80=94 HIGH =E2=80=
=94 BUILD/TEST

*Evidence:* House of Whiskerton markets its emailed digital portrait as
=E2=80=9CPerfect for a same-day gift=E2=80=9D; ArtWallzShop advertises 24-h=
our delivery;
Artify offers digital delivery immediately after approval. This strengthens
the previous last-minute review evidence with multiple current product
mechanisms.
*Wanted/problem:* buyer needs personalization despite having missed the
physical-delivery window.
*Current workaround:* emailed/downloadable portrait that can be forwarded
or printed locally.
*Roast.pet implication:* every physical order should immediately produce a
giftable digital reveal page/video; sell a Digital Roast as its own
last-minute SKU.
*Occasion:* forgotten birthday, same-day birthday, late Christmas purchase.
*Prototype:* dedicated Etsy title/thumbnail: =E2=80=9CForgot Their Birthday=
? Your
Dog Roasts Them Today =E2=80=94 Personalized Video=E2=80=9D. Test separatel=
y from physical
cards.
4. Important negative: some buyers explicitly reject digital/AI-style
substitutes =E2=80=94 MEDIUM =E2=80=94 WATCH

*Evidence:* A buyer in r/Etsy seeking a birthday portrait for their mother
explicitly said they were =E2=80=9CNot looking for anything digitally done.=
=E2=80=9D
Current portrait sellers also increasingly foreground =E2=80=9Chand-drawn=
=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9Creal
artists=E2=80=9D or =E2=80=9CI do NOT use AI=E2=80=9D.
*Problem:* for the traditional portrait/memorial job, digital generation
itself can reduce perceived authenticity.
*Current workaround:* commission graphite, gouache, cross-stitch,
hand-painted or other physical art.
*Roast.pet implication:* do NOT position Roast.pet as a superior pet
portrait or compete primarily on AI art quality. The differentiated job is
comedy/performance: the pet appears to speak/roast the recipient. Keep
memorial-with-humour on WATCH until direct buyer evidence appears;
sentimental memorial buyers may particularly value human-made artifacts.
*Prototype:* test copy emphasizing the outcome (=E2=80=9CYour dog roasts Da=
d=E2=80=9D) with
AI absent from the hero copy versus =E2=80=9CAI talking pet card=E2=80=9D.
Cluster state

*Strongest cumulative:* exact likeness/identity fidelity; preview/revision
assurance; fast/last-minute digital delivery; multi-pet;
pet-as-speaker/recipient-specific message; physical + QR/browser video.
*Supported but weaker:* editable front captions/jokes; humour/adult
pet-parent cards.
*UNKNOWN / insufficient direct demand:* mandatory AR, kid-safe mode,
adult-roast selector, sports roast, work-colleague roast,
memorial-with-humour.
TOP 5 CUSTOMER REQUESTS TO PRODUCTIZE

   1. Recognizable pet likeness with explicit identity-trait confirmation.
   2. Preview + painless corrections before fulfilment.
   3. Same-day digital/video delivery even when the physical card will
   arrive later.
   4. Multi-pet support without forcing separate purchases.
   5. Recipient-specific pet-as-speaker copy: pet talks directly to
   Mum/Dad/partner.

*Strongest unmet need:* combine high-confidence likeness + genuinely
personalized comedy + immediate delivery. Existing portrait products solve
likeness/revisions; existing funny cards solve humour; the gap remains
joining those with the pet performing the joke.

*Easiest ordering-flow conversion lift:* after upload, show an immediate
preview and ask the buyer to confirm 2=E2=80=934 identity-bearing traits be=
fore
payment/production. Make correction categories explicit rather than an
open-ended support message.

*Best new Etsy listing from actual language:* *=E2=80=9CForgot Dad=E2=80=99=
s Birthday? Your
Dog Roasts Him Today =E2=80=94 Personalized Pet Video + Printable Card=E2=
=80=9D*. This
directly combines demonstrated same-day gifting and established =E2=80=9Cca=
rd from
the dog=E2=80=9D behavior.

*Negative signal:* do not sell this as an AI replacement for commissioned
pet portraiture. Some gift buyers explicitly want non-digital work, and
multiple sellers use human-made/no-AI positioning as reassurance. Roast.pet
should own a different job: recognizable pet + personalized
comedy/performance.

Sources reviewed this run include Etsy, Reddit and current personalized-pet
product pages. No credible new direct customer-language evidence was found
for mandatory AR, sports-themed roast, kid/adult modes or
memorial-with-humour, so those remain UNKNOWN rather than inferred demand.

